{"id": "EUVD-2026-93174", "enisaUuid": "6c0912ce-ba34-3ee1-a165-d019b3e8b2d6", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sync: Serialize local codec list cleanup\n\nhci_dev_close_sync() clears hdev->local_codecs after releasing hdev->lock.\nCodec list additions and both traversals in sco_sock_getsockopt() use that\nlock, but the close path does not. A close and BT_CODEC query can therefore\ninterleave as follows:\n\n  hci_dev_close_sync()          sco_sock_getsockopt()\n                                hci_dev_lock()\n                                fetch codec entry\n  hci_codec_list_clear()\n    kfree(entry)\n                                read entry->id\n\nThe reader then accesses an entry which the close path has freed. KASAN\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in sco_sock_getsockopt+0xfa0/0xfe0\n  Read of size 1 at addr ffff8881001c3450\n  Call Trace:\n   sco_sock_getsockopt+0xfa0/0xfe0\n   do_sock_getsockopt+0x537/0x7b0\n   __sys_getsockopt+0xf2/0x170\n  Allocated by task 92:\n   hci_codec_list_add.isra.0+0x2c/0x440\n   hci_read_codec_capabilities+0x224/0x590\n   hci_read_supported_codecs+0x2c2/0x640\n  Freed by task 92:\n   kfree+0x131/0x3c0\n   hci_codec_list_clear+0xd8/0x160\n   hci_dev_close_sync+0x92a/0xfa0\n\nTake hdev->lock around the clear operation at its existing point in the\nclose path. This makes the clear wait for active readers and prevents a new\ntraversal until the list is empty without changing teardown ordering.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:16:17", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9f407d52c0d881430d689836d3e7d32aa36f98b5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/560ed4373c06a58123ecdf9ad5ecaddc87a73382", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ee0c5429dc4a92879bda2554b1bfd4abc6c587c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4dc1ae5ff75b17e17ec4b74b11cc4b0099e71e00", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1276c2fafd18499769a28f96f45c5a76d6fc990e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a10987a2f160a44a638c9a35994ca6e3089696e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98246", "GHSA-4jxq-xw37-v6h5"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20b776a6-dc83-3175-b087-73bb5fa268f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.5.7 <6.6"}, {"id": "22f40a0c-c19c-3d02-84cc-255765ef2b08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2ff2332e-87c5-30bf-a1fc-c4246ccaa3f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "5f2dacbd-be78-327a-95df-b54501a70f77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "6a16200c-7414-3657-a52a-31880f0b74d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b938790e70540bf4f2e653dcd74b232494d06c8f <4dc1ae5ff75b17e17ec4b74b11cc4b0099e71e00"}, {"id": "6d67d921-6b61-3b9b-bd5a-f5a2fd503b39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b938790e70540bf4f2e653dcd74b232494d06c8f <9a10987a2f160a44a638c9a35994ca6e3089696e"}, {"id": "6e08b76b-95a0-3b9d-ab5a-7ad2dbe2ffc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "7024d9e5-81f6-34c7-bfa5-73b20ae2e6c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eea5a8f0c3b7c884d2351e75fbdd0a3d7def5ae1"}, {"id": "71ab9c4a-50c5-3cab-8d79-8e2342877b13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "750d1163-6488-33f8-af9c-d7e905759609", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b938790e70540bf4f2e653dcd74b232494d06c8f <1276c2fafd18499769a28f96f45c5a76d6fc990e"}, {"id": "77b0bd03-b9ba-3f32-8d9d-bdc02589fd4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "a9dfa664-a54d-3afb-9068-0a8bfbb24622", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b938790e70540bf4f2e653dcd74b232494d06c8f <1ee0c5429dc4a92879bda2554b1bfd4abc6c587c"}, {"id": "bffbcdb1-c710-3ee7-9d80-63d39c0ef107", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c75b9629-8b06-3868-99d2-d7942804cb94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b938790e70540bf4f2e653dcd74b232494d06c8f <560ed4373c06a58123ecdf9ad5ecaddc87a73382"}, {"id": "cd747042-2252-3e52-9144-55841ad02171", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "626535077ba9dc110787540d1fe24881094c15a1 <9f407d52c0d881430d689836d3e7d32aa36f98b5"}, {"id": "d33e9397-0bff-3af4-88aa-5a82676f5bbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "ee099dc0-389a-3e3d-8830-67bf8a6dddcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.57 <6.1.189"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "451e5f3e-695b-3ef8-89b4-938848992380", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}